---
import FeatureCard from '../FeatureCard.astro';
---

<section class="features container">
  <div class="features__grid">
    <FeatureCard title="SQLite or PostgreSQL">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <ellipse cx="8" cy="5.5" rx="5" ry="2.2" />
        <path d="M3 5.5v5c0 1.2 2.24 2.2 5 2.2s5-1 5-2.2v-5" />
        <ellipse cx="16" cy="13.5" rx="5" ry="2.2" />
        <path d="M11 13.5v5c0 1.2 2.24 2.2 5 2.2s5-1 5-2.2v-5" />
      </svg>
      Embedded SQLite by default. Build with <code>-Dpostgres</code> and point <code>ZIGBASE_DB_URL</code> at a <code>postgres://</code> URL — same app, same API. <code>zigbase migrate-db</code> copies an existing instance across, schema and data.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Built for coding agents">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2" />
        <path d="M7 9.5l3 2.5-3 2.5" />
        <path d="M13 15h4" />
      </svg>
      Scaffold a project with <code>npx zigbase init</code> — a generated <code>AGENTS.md</code> included. <code>serve</code> backgrounds itself when it detects an agent shell, the CLI speaks <code>--json</code>, error codes are a frozen registry you can look up with <code>zigbase explain-code</code>, and any instance answers <code>GET /api/meta</code>.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Migrate an existing app">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <ellipse cx="6" cy="5.5" rx="4" ry="2" />
        <path d="M2 5.5v6c0 1.1 1.79 2 4 2s4-.9 4-2v-6" />
        <path d="M13 12h7" />
        <path d="M17.5 8.5L21 12l-3.5 3.5" />
      </svg>
      Declarative <code>schema dump</code>/<code>apply</code>, whole-dataset <code>import --manifest</code> that loads in relation order, and <code>--legacy-hashes bcrypt</code> so existing users keep their passwords — transparently rehashed to argon2id on first login. A parity-replay harness proves the cutover before you make it.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Collections & schema">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="8" ry="3" />
        <path d="M4 5v6c0 1.66 3.58 3 8 3s8-1.34 8-3V5" />
        <path d="M4 11v6c0 1.66 3.58 3 8 3s8-1.34 8-3v-6" />
      </svg>
      Typed fields with validation; schema migrations run on startup.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Multi-tenancy">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="4" y="3" width="10" height="18" rx="1" />
        <path d="M8 7h2M8 11h2M8 15h2" />
        <circle cx="17.5" cy="14" r="2.2" />
        <path d="M14 21c0-2 1.6-3.5 3.5-3.5S21 19 21 21" />
      </svg>
      Account-scoped collections: every read, write, and realtime delivery is bound to the request's active account, fail-closed. Built-in accounts, memberships, invitations, and roles.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Relationship abilities">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <circle cx="6" cy="6" r="2.5" />
        <circle cx="18" cy="6" r="2.5" />
        <circle cx="12" cy="18" r="2.5" />
        <path d="M8.5 6h7M7.2 8.2l3.6 7M16.8 8.2l-3.6 7" />
      </svg>
      Authorize by the caller's relationship to the row — <code>{'.{ .via = "account", .min_role = .editor }'}</code> — comptime-validated, fail-closed, and composed into list queries.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Full-text & vector search">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="6.5" />
        <path d="M16 16l5 5" />
        <path d="M8.5 11h5" />
      </svg>
      Mark a field <code>.searchable</code> and query <code>?search=</code> with ranked results — <code>AND</code>/<code>OR</code>/<code>NOT</code>/prefix operators on SQLite (FTS5); ranked <code>tsvector</code> search on Postgres. Opt-in <code>-Dvector</code> adds KNN via sqlite-vec / pgvector.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Background jobs & webhooks">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M4 6h10M4 12h10M4 18h10" />
        <path d="M17 9l4 3-4 3" />
      </svg>
      Durable or in-memory queues with priorities and retries; enqueue from anywhere with <code>ctx.enqueue()</code>. <code>ctx.webhook()</code> delivers signed, idempotent webhooks with capped backoff.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Transactional email">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2" />
        <path d="M3 7l9 6 9-6" />
      </svg>
      Multipart HTML+text templates, SES / Postmark / SMTP providers, verified per-account senders, bounce suppression — and a capture mailer for asserting mail in tests.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Product analytics">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M4 20h16" />
        <path d="M7 20v-6M12 20V9M17 20V5" />
      </svg>
      <code>ctx.track()</code> appends immutable events — actor, tenant, and timestamp stamped server-side. Declarative rollups aggregate them on the scheduler; tenant-scoped read API.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Realtime">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M5 12a7 7 0 0 1 14 0" />
        <path d="M8 12a4 4 0 0 1 8 0" />
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.5" />
        <path d="M12 13.5V21" />
      </svg>
      Subscribe to record changes over WebSocket + SSE, and broadcast on custom channels from routes and jobs. On Postgres, record changes fan out across app instances via LISTEN/NOTIFY.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Auth + OAuth2">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="11" rx="2" />
        <path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" />
        <circle cx="12" cy="15.5" r="1.4" />
      </svg>
      argon2id passwords, magic-link, OTP, and WebAuthn passkeys; OAuth2 with PKCE and account linking. Hook <code>beforeAuthSuccess</code> and <code>.auth.beforeRegister</code> transactionally with login and registration.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="File storage">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M14 3H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9z" />
        <path d="M14 3v6h6" />
        <path d="M9 14h6M9 17h4" />
      </svg>
      Local (pluggable) file storage with short-lived file-access tokens.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Single static binary">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2" />
        <path d="M7 9l3 3-3 3" />
        <path d="M13 15h4" />
      </svg>
      One executable, no runtime dependencies — the Postgres driver is pure Zig (no libpq, no OpenSSL).
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Embeddable Zig framework">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M13 2 4 14h6l-1 8 9-12h-6z" />
      </svg>
      Comptime hooks, custom routes, scheduled jobs, and plugins.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Static file serving">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="14" rx="2" />
        <path d="M3 8h18" />
        <path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" />
      </svg>
      Ship your frontend from the same binary — point a flag at a folder, or embed it at compile time.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Typed client SDKs">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M4 6h16M4 12h10M4 18h7" />
        <path d="M16 16l3 3 5-6" transform="translate(-2 -3)" />
      </svg>
      Official TypeScript, Dart, Python, and Kotlin SDKs. Generate a fully-typed client from your Zig schema — records, realtime, files, and typed custom-route RPC. No Zig source? Bootstrap types from any running instance with <code>npx @zigbase/typegen</code>.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Session management">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4" />
        <path d="M4 20c0-4 3.6-7 8-7s8 3 8 7" />
        <path d="M17 14l2 2 4-3" transform="translate(-3 0)" />
      </svg>
      Revoke all sessions instantly via epoch rotation. Optional per-device session table: list active sessions, revoke one device, or log out everywhere.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Rate limiting & CAPTCHA">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
        <path d="M12 7v5l3 3" />
      </svg>
      Global rate limiter plus per-auth-method limits — set each method's <code>.rate_limit</code> option at comptime, or call <code>ac.rateLimit()</code> from a custom auth method at runtime. And <code>ctx.verifyCaptcha()</code> for reCAPTCHA, hCaptcha, and Turnstile.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Field encryption">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="11" rx="2" />
        <path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" />
        <path d="M12 15v2" />
      </svg>
      Mark any text/JSON field <code>encrypted</code> for transparent AES-256-GCM at rest. Rotate keys with <code>zigbase rewrap</code> — old generations stay readable while you re-encrypt.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="TTL & KV store">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M3 6h18M3 12h18M3 18h18" />
        <circle cx="19" cy="6" r="2" fill="currentColor" />
      </svg>
      Auto-expiring records via <code>.ttl_field</code> (GC'd every 5 min). Built-in KV store for feature flags and settings, surfaced in the admin UI.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Ctx capability layer">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="3" y="3" width="8" height="8" rx="1" />
        <rect x="13" y="3" width="8" height="8" rx="1" />
        <rect x="3" y="13" width="8" height="8" rx="1" />
        <rect x="13" y="13" width="8" height="8" rx="1" />
      </svg>
      A single <code>*Ctx</code> handed to every hook, route, and job — wraps records, auth, KV, flags, outbound HTTP, and atomic transactions. One handle for your app's capabilities — pooled DB access, <code>track</code>, <code>enqueue</code>, <code>mail</code>, <code>webhook</code> — no globals.
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard title="Deterministic testing">
      <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M9 3H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v4m6-6h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4M9 3v18m0 0h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9M9 21H5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2V9m0 0h18" />
      </svg>
      Freeze time with <code>ZIGBASE_FAKE_NOW</code>, fix randomness with <code>ZIGBASE_FAKE_SEED</code>, and capture outbound mail in test suites — all gated off in production builds.
    </FeatureCard>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .features {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
  }

  .features__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
